{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:11:42Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 30, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t## Test verification \u2014 Taiga #4: Give tasks a priority\n2\t\n3\t**Commands actually run this session:**\n4\t- `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 **22 passed** (14 pre-existing + 8 new: `test_create_defaults_to_normal_priority`, `test_create_with_explicit_priority`, `test_create_with_invalid_priority_is_rejected`, `test_updating_priority_changes_it`, `test_updating_priority_does_not_change_title_id_or_done`, `test_updating_priority_of_a_missing_task_is_404`, `test_updating_priority_with_invalid_value_is_rejected`, `test_updating_title_leaves_priority_untouched`). Full suite, not just new tests.\n5\t- `cd frontend && npm run build` \u2192 succeeds (vite build, 20 modules, no errors).\n6\t- `npm test` \u2192 `npm error Missing script: \"test\"` \u2014 confirms this project has **no frontend test framework configured**, despite `CLAUDE.md` documenting `npm test` as the frontend test command. Pre-existing gap, not introduced by this feature.\n7\t\n8\t**Not run, and why:** `npm run lint`, starting the backend/frontend dev servers, and even a standalone `node` check \u2014 all required interactive approval this non-interactive session has no channel to grant (same limitation the prior review stage hit). No live-browser exercise of the feature was possible.\n9\t\n10\t**Verified by reading code + hand-tracing logic (not execution), since no frontend harness exists to automate it:**\n11\t- AC5/6/9 (stable high-first sort): `App.jsx:33-35` \u2014 `[...visibleTasks].sort((a,b) => (a.priority==='high'?0:1) - (b.priority==='high'?0:1))`. Traced by hand against the spec's literal example `[A:normal, B:high, C:low, D:high, E:normal]`: comparator keys are `[1,0,1,0,1]`; a stable sort (guaranteed by ECMA-262 since ES2019, universal in evergreen engines) on those keys yields `[B, D, A, C, E]` \u2014 matches the spec exactly.\n12\t- AC7 (sort scoped to filtered subset): `visibleTasks` (filter) computed first, `sortedTasks` derived from it \u2014 a filtered-out Done task can't reappear via the sort.\n13\t- AC8 (priority visible without edit mode): `TaskList.jsx:93-103`, view-mode branch always renders the `priority-select`.\n14\t- AC1-4, AC10: covered directly by the passing backend tests above.\n15\t\n16\t**Findings:** none new. I confirm the three items the prior review already surfaced (`TaskIn` still accepting an ignored `priority` on `PATCH /api/tasks/{id}`; `PRIORITIES` duplicated across `AddTask.jsx`/`TaskList.jsx`; `docs/spec.md` stale) \u2014 all are quality/documentation issues, not violations of any acceptance criterion, and none reproduce as a test failure.\n17\t\n18\t**Unverified, disclosed rather than assumed:** actual browser rendering/interaction (badge colors, select-triggers-immediate-update, filter+sort together in a live DOM) \u2014 blocked by sandbox approval limits, not by any defect found. Given no failures surfaced anywhere I could run or reason through, and the gap is an environment limitation rather than a code problem:\n19\t\n20\tVERDICT: pass", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01W6B4CZVpruPm62fVJBZjrg", "session_id": "1966a27b-a316-4c06-9e9f-d851bcfae3f0"}}
