{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:13:01Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 118, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\tThis matches the design (`PATCH /api/tasks/{id}/priority` per `docs/design.md:176-178`). Backend implementation is complete and verified.\n2\t\n3\t## Backend handoff summary\n4\t\n5\t**Files changed:**\n6\t- `backend/app/models.py` \u2014 added `Priority = Literal[\"low\", \"normal\", \"high\"]`; `TaskIn` and `Task` gained `priority: Priority = \"normal\"`; added `PriorityIn` (single-field model for the priority-update endpoint). Invalid values are rejected with `422` automatically via Pydantic's `Literal` validation \u2014 no manual check needed.\n7\t- `backend/app/store.py` \u2014 `TaskStore.add()` takes an optional `priority` (default `\"normal\"`); added `set_priority()` mirroring the existing `set_done()` shape.\n8\t- `backend/app/main.py` \u2014 `create_task` passes `payload.priority` through; added `PATCH /api/tasks/{task_id}/priority` (matches `docs/design.md`'s `api.js` contract \u2014 note this uses `PATCH`, not `POST` like `/done`, since that's what the design doc's frontend call already specifies).\n9\t- `backend/tests/test_tasks.py` \u2014 8 new tests: default priority on create, explicit priority on create, invalid priority rejected on create (no mutation), priority update, priority update leaves title/id/done untouched, 404 on missing task, invalid priority rejected on update (no mutation), title update leaves priority untouched.\n10\t\n11\t**Verification:** `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 22 passed (14 pre-existing + 8 new). Two pre-existing, unrelated warnings (httpx2 deprecation notice, pytest cache write permission).\n12\t\n13\t**Deviation from spec draft:** the inline spec said \"mirrors the existing `/done` action-scoped route\" (implying `POST`), but `docs/design.md`'s frontend `api.js` snippet explicitly calls `PATCH .../priority`. I followed the design doc since it's the more concrete, later-stage artifact \u2014 flagging in case that was an unintentional mismatch between stages.\n14\t\n15\t**Known gap:** `docs/spec.md` on disk still holds the prior cycle's content (per both earlier stages' notes) \u2014 I did not touch it, since resolving that overwrite was called out as needing user confirmation first.\n16\t\n17\tFrontend scope (api.js, AddTask.jsx, TaskList.jsx, App.jsx, App.css) is out of my scope and untouched.", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01RqRdsYhLujW2mycNAcEGoC", "session_id": "1966a27b-a316-4c06-9e9f-d851bcfae3f0"}}
