{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:13:17Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 133, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t`docs/design.md` is written. Summary for the next stage:\n2\t\n3\t**Key decisions:**\n4\t- One `<select className=\"priority-select priority-{level}\">` per row (and in `AddTask`) does double duty as both the at-a-glance indicator and the change control \u2014 no separate badge, no new dropdown component.\n5\t- `normal` = baseline styling (blends in), `high` = solid orange fill `#a8480a`/white text (5.84:1 contrast, computed \u2014 deliberately not reusing `.error`'s red to keep \"red = error\" unambiguous), `low` = light gray `#e8eaec`/`#4a545c` text (6.42:1), with a border since the fill alone is only 1.21:1 against the white card.\n6\t- Priority change applies immediately on select (no Save step), same precedent as `Done` and `TaskFilter`.\n7\t- Sort is a stable partition (`high` first) applied to `App.jsx`'s already-filtered `visibleTasks`, not the raw list \u2014 satisfies the filter-then-sort ordering the spec requires.\n8\t- No optimistic UI \u2014 reuses the existing `run()`/`refresh()` pattern verbatim, so a failed change just snaps the select back to server state via the existing controlled-component wiring.\n9\t\n10\t**Flag for you:** `docs/spec.md` on disk still holds the prior cycle's \"Edit a task title\" content \u2014 the Taiga #4 spec I designed against was only given inline in this dispatch, pending your confirmation to overwrite it and to resolve the interleaved-vs-3-tier sort question. Worth confirming both and persisting `docs/spec.md` before the developer stage starts, so it isn't building from a stale file.", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_012jWtiyy2Bm4HFnnTZM9sZM", "session_id": "1966a27b-a316-4c06-9e9f-d851bcfae3f0"}}
