{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:13:25Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 137, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "Edit", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01AKQNn8eR7tYkqVjN19LbQu", "input": {"replace_all": false, "file_path": "/home/dev/projects/ai-dev-switchboard/agents/tester.md", "old_string": "4. **Exercise the feature for real** if it has a user-visible dimension. If\n   the project has browser automation available, drive the actual interface:\n   the states the design specified, not just the happy path.\n5. **Push on the boundaries**: empty and null input, duplicates, concurrent\n   operations, permission boundaries \u2014 can one user reach another's data? \u2014\n   and anything the story flagged as platform-specific.", "new_string": "4. **Exercise the feature for real** if it has a user-visible dimension. If\n   the project has browser automation available, drive the actual interface:\n   the states the design specified, not just the happy path.\n5. **Push on the boundaries**: empty and null input, duplicates, concurrent\n   operations, permission boundaries \u2014 can one user reach another's data? \u2014\n   and anything the story flagged as platform-specific.\n\nIf a tool call is denied for lack of an interactive approval channel \u2014 a\nbackground server launch, or an edit to a file the sandbox won't clear \u2014\n**do not retry the identical call.** This session is non-interactive; nobody\nis there to grant it on the second or third try either, so retrying only\nburns the attempt. Fall back immediately to whatever verification your\nexisting rights do allow (the pre-existing test suite, a build, hand-tracing\nthe changed code against each acceptance criterion), same as the reviewer\nstage already does when it hits the same wall, and disclose exactly what went\nunverified and why. That is a `pass` with a stated gap, not a stall."}, "session_id": "1966a27b-a316-4c06-9e9f-d851bcfae3f0"}}
